---
title: "Notes"
description: "A page whose own bibliography is laid over the project-wide one."
bibliography: local.bib
---

## Overriding a shared entry

This page declares its own `bibliography: local.bib`, which is merged **over**
the project-wide `references.bib` rather than replacing it. Two things follow.

A key defined in both resolves to *this page's* entry, so [@turing1950] renders
the corrected reprint rather than the shared record. That is how a post fixes or
sharpens one reference without editing the file every other page reads.

A key defined only locally still resolves, so [@hamming1950] works here and
nowhere else.
